  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **Built against `LazyCE` in Compze.Threading, where it moved from Compze.Internals.SystemCE, and against SystemCE's `WithAggregateExceptionsAsync`, which was `WithAggregateExceptions`:** the released version uses both where they were, and would fail beside the new packages with a `TypeLoadException` or a `MissingMethodException`.\n- **`InterprocessEndpointRegistry.RetractEndpointAddress` retracts only the address this process announced,** and a new overload retracts the one a given process announced. Before, it removed the endpoint's address whichever process had announced it. So a process that handed its endpoint over to a successor, which announced the endpoint under the same id while the old process still ran, removed the successor's address as it stopped, and nothing listed the endpoint until the successor announced again: routers dropped it, and sends to it waited out their patience and failed.\n- **Requires newer minor versions of other Compze packages:** Compze.DependencyInjection 0.10.0-alpha (was 0.9.0-alpha), Compze.Internals.SystemCE 0.10.0-internal (was 0.8.0-internal), Compze.InterprocessObject 0.10.0-alpha (was 0.9.0-alpha), Compze.Tessaging 0.11.0-alpha (was 0.9.0-alpha), Compze.Threading 0.13.0-alpha (was 0.12.0-alpha). Upgrading to this version upgrades each package listed here too, so their changelogs apply to this upgrade as well.",
